WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.920
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and because comic
con put me behind this is going to be my Teen

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.349
Wolf episode 6 and 7 video. I’m mostly going
to focus on Episode 7 just because there was

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:17.349
some really important stuff but I will mention
the really important takeaways from last week.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.680
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I do Teen Wolf every week. Be sure to

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.770
subscribe to get everything. At the end of
this video I’ll say who won the comic con

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.080
giveaway.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.820
So let’s get going. Careful for spoilers
from episodes 6 and 7 if you haven’t seen

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.530
them yet. I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here
we go.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:43.079
Most important stuff from episode 6. Peter
and Kate are going to be working together.

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:46.470
Kate controls the Berserkers but it seems
like neither she or Peter are connected to

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.649
the Benefactor in a conscious way.

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:52.130
Previously I had thought Peter was a good
candidate as a way to get his Alpha powers

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:57.170
back but now it seems like he’s just one
of the victims and is making lemonade with

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.420
all the lemons trying to kill him.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:06.420
Meredith flips her shit when Lydia presses
her for the last cypher key, but before she

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:11.920
killed herself she said “he doesn’t want
me to tell you”. Meaning she has been in

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.920
communication with whoever he is. Notice she
said “he” too, so it’s not a woman.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:24.610
And Derek being the last cypher key was a
pretty big WTF. They said it was someone who

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:29.020
would be dead. So the last portion of the
list hasn’t been circulated to all the mercenaries.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:35.470
The whole messages on a mixtape thing is a
bit strange and I wonder if the Benefactor

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:40.470
is using that old timey method of communication
to stay off the net or if it’s an affectation.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.960
Like him circulating the tapes ties in to
his character traits.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.280
Moving on to Episode 7, I’m going to do
this just like I normally do with TOP 5 WTF

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.259
Moments and a longer review. So here we go.

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:49.590
Number 5 - Satomi isn’t Dead

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:53.470
I loved her introduction. It was straight
out of a Kung Fu fight movie. Slow Motion

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.960
martial arts fight in heavy rain. This reminded
me of a movie called The Grandmaster, that’s

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:05.479
about IP Man one of the real life greatest
Kung Fu masters to ever live. The whole opening

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:07.579
scene of that movie is an epic battle in the
rain.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:10.619
It’s on netflix so you should watch it immediately

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:16.380
It feels like she’s going to become a bigger
part of the story this season and help them

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.640
take down the benefactor. I could definitely
see her sacrificing herself for Scott’s

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:24.770
pack. Her own pack is all dead, so unless
she creates a new beta or starts working with

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:31.770
Derek there’s not a lot left for her to
do on the show.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:35.860
Number 4 - Coach Used to be a Drunk

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:41.000
So this was the backne reveal. That’s what
I thought when she pulled his shirt up. If

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.020
you were confused about how the virus worked.
It would put everyone down for a little while.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.680
But non-were creatures would just automatically
get better after a short period of time.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.510
So that’s why coach just shot up and asked
what the hell was going on.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.140
Lydia’s Mom was so cool during this. Most
of the time when we see her she’s being

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:59.300
completely ridiculous. But we find out when
things start to slide downhill that she really

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:06.300
cares about everyone, especially coach. Who
I guess used to be a crazy drunk?

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.280
Alcohol and substance abuse are big problems
for celebrities or athletes that get their

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:17.080
careers torpedoed by injuries. Remember, Coach
was a big athlete that just never made it.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.900
I can’t remember if they explained why.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:28.220
I always love it when they reveal big character
details for minor characters. And how cute

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.150
was it that when Lydia came in her mother
immediately pretended to be ridiculous again.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:38.200
I think she did that just to make Lydia feel
more comfortable.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.360
Number 3 - Stiles Wants to Keep The Money

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.860
This got pretty dark. It almost made me think
Stiles was in on the Deadpool list somehow.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:50.940
Just the language that he used. And how passionate
he got about not rushing to give the money

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.670
over to Peter and Derek.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:57.019
Even Scott was confused by his behavior. The
Eichenhouse money thing has been teased this

00:03:57.019 --> 00:04:01.080
season just like Scott’s Mom going bankrupt
and losing the house.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:06.709
There’s two practical outcomes. The hero
option, Stiles and Scott just suck it up,

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:11.299
give the money over to Derek and look for
overtime work to help pay off their debts.

00:04:11.299 --> 00:04:16.220
Heroes don’t steal. Think of it like “What
would Captain America do?”

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:23.220
The 
other morally ambiguous option is that they
give Derek part of the money and keep the

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:27.689
other half to pay the bills.

00:04:27.689 --> 00:04:30.990
Because of the trust issues going on with
Malia in the episode I don’t see Stiles

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:35.389
pushing as hard for this. If he took the money
and Peter found out, it would just be more

00:04:35.389 --> 00:04:38.169
ammo to drive a wedge between Malia and the
pack.

00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:41.659
Eventually Peter is going to surround himself
with more allies as he grows more powerful.

00:04:41.659 --> 00:04:46.300
So he’s going to try and coerce Malia at
some point. If she doesn’t just rush over

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.189
to the loft immediately for answers.

00:04:48.189 --> 00:04:53.249
Number 2 - PSAT Guy is Infecting Everyone

00:04:53.249 --> 00:05:00.249
As crazy as him holding the gun against Stiles
head I think that guy’s introduction in

00:05:02.319 --> 00:05:08.099
the creepy basement was worse. If you weren’t
sure what he was doing, he was testing the

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:12.020
virus to see how long it took to kill a werewolf.
That’s why he left that guy on the hospital

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.189
bed inside the ring of mountain ash.

00:05:14.189 --> 00:05:18.039
The whole virus subplot was an interesting
homage to Cabin Fever or any infection movie

00:05:18.039 --> 00:05:18.550
you can think of. I’m a bigger fan of movies
that take place in the aftermath of big outbreaks,

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:22.539
like Walking Dead. But I like how Teen Wolf
can do genres within genres.

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:27.069
It’s a show about werewolves first, but
getting meta with other genres just gives

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:29.110
you so many places to go with stories.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:33.830
It seems like a lot of these deapool mercenaries
get one episode arcs, or really short ones.

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:38.439
There’s only a few episodes left, so I wonder
if the mercenaries we run into next will just

00:05:38.439 --> 00:05:41.550
be progressively bigger and badder until we
get to that final boss fight.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:47.020
Like Scott’s pack is playing Mike Tyson’s
Punch Out and they just have to get through

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.569
all the bosses before they can fight Mike
Tyson.

00:05:49.569 --> 00:05:53.889
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - Malia Learns
the Truth about Peter

00:05:53.889 --> 00:05:57.899
I was pretty surprised by the way she found
out. I had expected her and Stiles relationship

00:05:57.899 --> 00:06:01.999
to not be a part of the reveal. But we always
knew she’d find out at some point. And then

00:06:01.999 --> 00:06:04.999
they did the whole ‘hiding things’ moment
with Kira.

00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:10.819
The big question now is what will she do after
she gets the full story from Peter and will

00:06:10.819 --> 00:06:14.699
Peter create some fiction to keep her close.
It seems like Scott and the others would have

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:19.020
explained Peter to her. Mostly that he can’t
be trusted and he’s a terrible person.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:26.020
That’s the logical thing, but at Comic Con
when someone asked Jeff Davis about Malia

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:33.159
learning to do her hair and makeup, he waved
his hand and said TV Rules. He was pretty

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:38.399
open about saying the writers hoped fans would
give them a pass at the logic of Malia learning

00:06:38.399 --> 00:06:40.909
to be a normal girl.

00:06:40.909 --> 00:06:46.279
For the most part I don’t mind, but I hope
they don’t wave their hands too much at

00:06:46.279 --> 00:06:49.259
the logic when it comes to Peter and Malia.
She’s pissed about Scott and the other’s

00:06:49.259 --> 00:06:53.259
not telling her the truth, but that shouldn’t
make her forget what an awful person Peter

00:06:53.259 --> 00:06:56.249
is.
But let me know what your biggest WTF from

00:06:56.249 --> 00:07:00.550
the episode was and do you think that Malia
will go be with Peter or will she just run

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.459
off into the woods?

00:07:01.459 --> 00:07:05.249
I think the show teased us way too much with
a Peter Malia moment so I definitely think

00:07:05.249 --> 00:07:09.479
we’ll see that. But I think in the end,
Malia will betray Peter to help Stiles and

00:07:09.479 --> 00:07:10.539
the pack before the end.

00:07:10.539 --> 00:07:14.659
Whatever ends up happening with the Benefactor,
Peter will have his own side scheme. It will

00:07:14.659 --> 00:07:21.659
probably involve dicking over Derek and everyone
else. And I feel like Malia will do the right

00:07:22.649 --> 00:07:28.360
thing when she’s put in a situation where
she has to choose.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:35.360
I mean she’s gotta come back 
before season 5, who’s going going to spoon
stiles? Maybe Derek I guess?

00:07:41.279 --> 00:07:45.559
They actually did that in an episode of family
guy, where Peter and Quagmire have to spoon

00:07:45.559 --> 00:07:47.599
because Lois doesn’t want to anymore.

00:07:47.599 --> 00:07:51.669
Overall I gave the episode a solid B. It had
a couple of great left turns with Satomi and

00:07:51.669 --> 00:07:56.569
Malia. Stiles just got way more complicated.
Scott is the Captain America of the group,

00:07:56.569 --> 00:08:00.379
he’ll always try to do the right thing.
Stiles on the other hand feels like Bucky.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.149
He’s even been brainwashed before like Bucky
during season 3b.

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:06.969
Wouldn’t it be crazy if Stiles and Scott
had a falling out over the money. This season

00:08:06.969 --> 00:08:10.459
is supposed to be all about human issues.
And fighting over money is a very human thing

00:08:10.459 --> 00:08:10.819
to do.

00:08:10.819 --> 00:08:14.989
I also really like how they paired people
up in this episode. Like putting Derek with

00:08:14.989 --> 00:08:18.009
Braeden, Lydia’s Mom with the students,
Malia and Kira.

00:08:18.009 --> 00:08:22.259
I tend to favor the light and funny stories.
Like the Lacrosse stuff, Malia trying to be

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:29.259
human, Scott and Kira relationship humor.
Lydia and Deputy Parrish. So when we get more

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:33.990
intense episodes like this one I always look
really hard for the lighter moments. Like

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:38.779
the Satomi reveal. It swung from crazy Hong
Kong fight movie to hey what’s up in a few

00:08:38.779 --> 00:08:39.069
seconds.

00:08:39.069 --> 00:08:40.360
And Kira fumbling over her words when it comes
to her and Scott. It’s like the whole episode

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:43.769
was a slow heart attack, so fun moments like
those are very appreciated.

00:08:43.769 --> 00:08:47.490
And since it is the halfway point of the season
I feel like all the remaining episodes are

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.149
going to be a slow heart attack.

00:08:49.149 --> 00:08:53.029
Let me know if you guys agree, do you like
the fun episodes more or do you like it more

00:08:53.029 --> 00:09:00.029
when things get intense and you feel like
your heart is going to burst inside your chest?

